    <imageSet>
        <name>Unaligned multi-frame micrographs of tetrahymena ribozyme.</name>
        <directory>/data/ThR/exposures</directory>
        <category>micrographs - multiframe</category>
        <headerFormat>TIFF</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>TIFF</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>18366</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>30</framesPerImage>
        <voxelType>UNSIGNED BYTE</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>5760</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>0.82</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>4092</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>0.82</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>These micrographs were collected with a Titan Krios G3i, 300kV and a K3 detector. Over the collection, the sample was exposed evenly to 57.25 electrons per angstrom squared with a total exposure time of 2.5 seconds. Desired defocuses ranged from -0.5 to -2 nm. The exposures are not gain corrected, the gain reference can be found at data/ThR/exposures/K3-18210041 Gain Ref. x1.m1.mrc.</details>
        <segmentationList/>
        <micrographsFilePattern>data/ThR/exposures/GridSquare_*/*_fractions.tiff</micrographsFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesFilePattern></pickedParticlesFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesDirectory></pickedParticlesDirectory>
    </imageSet>
